A||N||1||GT-maniac||Fuel injector cleaning||||5||
Z||000000||GT-maniac||10-18-2001||10:53 AM||||Does anyone know the difference between a fuel injector purge and a fuel injector cleaning such as that offered by my local lube shop ? The purge is about twice the cost and I'm wondering if it's worth it. I'm hoping to remedy a lack of power and poor fuel economy which I think is caused by dirty injectors.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero005a.jpg"> <P>85 WS6 GT partly modified<BR>87 GT Loaded resto project||||reg||5
Z||000001||Alex4mula||10-18-2001||01:29 PM||||The root cause to your problem could be many things which all add up to that. Anyway, if you want to clean the injectors the best investment is to take them out and send for cleanning/blueprinting. They will kind of rebuilt them and test flow them and tell you if they are ok. Cost from $10-$20 per injector depending the place. So instead of paying like $50 for a liquid clean you may be able to get a better treatment and better results if you invest a little more.||||reg||1
